{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2lel83b","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"physics","chapter":"properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"pressure-density-pascals-law-and-archimedes-principle","type":"mcqm","marks":4,"negMarks":2,"permalink":"ptwo-solid-spheres-a-and-b-of-equal-volumes-but-of-differe-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-jc7g0uohtqrz2tqx","content":"<p>Two solid spheres A and B of equal volumes but of different densities d<sub>A</sub> and d<sub>B</sub> are connected by a string. They are fully immersed in a fluid of density d<sub>F</sub>. They get arranged into an equilibrium state as shown in the figure with a tension in the string. The arrangement is possible only if</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Properties of Matter Question 20 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l2mkuwuo/bd1760f2-e07f-4ae7-9d10-bb1ad686e6ae/dd3ccd00-c8e8-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2mkuwup.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"d<sub>A</sub> < d<sub>F</sub>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"d<sub>B</sub> > d<sub>F</sub>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"d<sub>A</sub> > d<sub>F</sub>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"d<sub>A</sub> + d<sub>B</sub> = 2d<sub>F</sub>"}],"correct_options":["A","B","D"],"explanation":"<p>Let V be the volume of each sphere and let T be the tension in the string.</p>\n<p>Buoyant force on sphere A is U<sub>A</sub> = d<sub>F</sub>Vg</p>\n<p>Buoyant force on sphere B is U<sub>B</sub> = d<sub>F</sub>Vg</p>\n<p>Weight of A is W<sub>A</sub> = d<sub>A</sub>Vg</p>\n<p>Weight of B is W<sub>B</sub> = d<sub>B</sub>Vg</p>\n<p>The free body diagrams of A and B are as follows. (see Fig. 11.34)</p>\n<p>For equilibrium,</p>\n<p>U<sub>A</sub> = T + W<sub>A</sub> and U<sub>B</sub> + T = W<sub>B</sub></p>\n<p>i.e. d<sub>F</sub>Vg = T + d<sub>A</sub>Vg ..... (i)</p>\n<p>and d<sub>F</sub>Vg + T = d<sub>B</sub>Vg .... (ii)</p>\n<p>From Eq. (i) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.108ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.903ex\" height=\"3.083ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -872.7 6145.1 1362.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D439\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D439\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1410.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2466.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(408.1,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(769,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1083.2\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4011.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5011.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-152.7) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Hence, d<sub>F</sub> &gt; d<sub>A</sub>. So choice (a) is correct.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Properties of Matter Question 20 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l2ml18kb/5df75cce-7990-49d2-91e0-d215ab13af3b/8d23c6b0-c8e9-11ec-8c2d-13f33da2fbe1/file-1l2ml18kc.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>From Eq. (ii) <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.108ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.917ex\" height=\"3.083ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -872.7 6151.5 1362.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1417.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2473.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(408.1,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(769,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D454\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D454\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1083.2\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4018.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5018.9,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D439\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D439\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. Hence d<sub>B</sub> &gt; d<sub>F</sub>. So choice (b) is also correct.</p>\n<p>Eliminating T from Eqs. (i) and (ii) we get <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.345ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"14.619ex\" height=\"1.916ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 6461.6 846.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D439\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D439\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1910.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2966.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-152.7) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4321.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5322,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D451\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D451\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(553,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, which is choice (d).</p>\n<p>So, the correct choices are (a), (b) and (d).</p>"}]}